Subject: [PATCH] phar: fix use-after-free in phar_call_openssl_signverify()

In the IS_BOOL case, retval_ptr was efree()d and then read with
Z_BVAL_P() to decide success. Read the result first. This path is used
when phar signs through userland openssl_sign() (PHAR_HAVE_OPENSSL not
defined), e.g. Phar::setSignatureAlgorithm(Phar::OPENSSL).

Lab (build container, gcc 16): under valgrind, phar/tar/zip
phar_setsignaturealgo2.phpt go from LEAK ("Invalid read of size 1" right
after _efree) to PASS; test_signaturealgos PASS on both. phpt
ext/openssl+ftp+phar against OpenSSL 4.1.0: fail list identical to the
unfixed build (43 each).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/phar/util.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/phar/util.c b/ext/phar/util.c
index 06e4e55d..f1eeb2f0 100644
--- a/ext/phar/util.c
+++ b/ext/phar/util.c
@@ -1500,9 +1500,12 @@ static int phar_call_openssl_signverify(int is_sign, php_stream *fp, off_t end,
 			}
 			efree(retval_ptr);
 			return FAILURE;
-		case IS_BOOL:
+		case IS_BOOL: {
+			/* read the result before freeing the zval that holds it */
+			zend_bool ok = Z_BVAL_P(retval_ptr);
+
 			efree(retval_ptr);
-			if (Z_BVAL_P(retval_ptr)) {
+			if (ok) {
 				*signature = estrndup(Z_STRVAL_P(zsig), Z_STRLEN_P(zsig));
 				*signature_len = Z_STRLEN_P(zsig);
 				zval_dtor(zsig);
@@ -1512,6 +1515,7 @@ static int phar_call_openssl_signverify(int is_sign, php_stream *fp, off_t end,
 			zval_dtor(zsig);
 			efree(zsig);
 			return FAILURE;
+		}
 	}
 }
 /* }}} */
From 80bc442cd0d67680350972f532822bd49cebdae9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:46:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6 (CVE-2026-129289): drain unread
 FastCGI request bodies

Backport of php-src c7a30157f6 ("Fix GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6: Drain unread
request bodies", PHP-8.2).

Opening php://input creates SG(request_info).request_body without
consuming the body from the SAPI; sapi_deactivate() took the stream as
proof the body was read and skipped the drain, so unread FastCGI STDIN
bytes could be parsed as a new request on an FCGI_KEEP_CONN connection.
Drain whenever post_read is false, and refuse a new FastCGI request if
the previous STDIN record was only partially consumed.

Differences from upstream:
- main/SAPI.c: same hunk (sapi_deactivate instead of
  sapi_deactivate_module).
- 5.6 has no main/fastcgi.c. FPM has its own sapi/fpm/fpm/fastcgi.c and
  php-cgi its own sapi/cgi/fastcgi.c; both get the two fastcgi.c hunks.
  fcgi_read_request(): plain `if (req->in_len != 0)` (no UNEXPECTED),
  before the `closed` (8.x: `ended`) reset. fcgi_close(): in_len = 0
  right after `req->fd = -1;` (FPM: before fpm_request_finished(); CGI:
  after the TCP_NODELAY block, there is no on_close hook in 5.6).
- Tests: upstream unread-body-keep-conn.phpt and
  unread-body-partial-record.phpt rewritten for the 5.6 FPM test
  harness (include.inc/run_fpm, no FPM\Tester, no typed params, arrow
  fns or str_contains); shared raw FastCGI helpers in
  sapi/fpm/tests/ghsa-qc49-hpvq-g2w6.inc.

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
