Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j (CVE-2026-128064): mixed-case HTTPS
 and FTPS URLs use TLS

Backport of php-src 9c0b44ffd6 ("Fix GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j: mixed case
HTTPS and FTPS", PHP-8.2).

The http and ftp wrappers decided on TLS by checking for a lower-case
's' at scheme[4] / scheme[3], so HTTPS:// and FTPS:// URLs (accepted by
the case-insensitive wrapper lookup) were sent in plaintext, including
credentials and request bodies. Compare the whole scheme
case-insensitively.

Differences from upstream:
- 5.6 resource->scheme is char*, not zend_string: strcasecmp() instead
  of zend_string_equals_literal_ci(); the NULL guard is kept in both
  wrappers (upstream drops it in the http wrapper).
- Tests: both upstream tests adapted to the 5.6 ServerClientTestCase
  (no {{ ADDR }} or phpt_notify(message:)): the server binds port 0 and
  passes its address and result through files in sys_get_temp_dir();
  str_contains -> strpos; openssl checked in SKIPIF instead of
  --EXTENSIONS--.

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
