Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg (CVE-2026-15353): out-of-bounds read
 on empty SOAP-ENC:arraySize

Backport of php-src 382d249480 ("Fix GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg: out-of-bounds
read on empty SOAP-ENC:arraySize", PHP-8.2).

calc_dimension_12() returned 0 for an empty or digit-less arraySize
(from a request or from a WSDL), and the callers then walked a
zero-length position/dimension array. Treat it as one dimension.

Differences from upstream: none in C (same one-line hunk). Tests:
GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg.phpt and GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg-wsdl.phpt rewritten
for 5.6 syntax (no typed params/return types, constructor promotion,
flexible heredoc, `??` or str_contains); soap checked in SKIPIF. The
.wsdl is unchanged.

Not compiled or tested yet.

