From 3c0e923fe12e986076439ff7ea1a50fea506725e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:52:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-4646-p932-gw34 (CVE-2026-129506): keep SOAP DTD
 alive during cleanup

Backport of php-src 13a0f8c8c1 ("Fix GHSA-4646-p932-gw34: keep SOAP DTD
alive during cleanup", PHP-8.2).

cleanup_xml_node() unlinked and freed every non-element child of the
document, including the internal DTD. Attribute values with entity
references can share content with the DTD's entity declarations, so the
freed DTD left dangling pointers that were read later (use-after-free).
Leave the DTD node in place; it is freed with the document. As a side
effect the existing "DTD are not supported by SOAP" check in
SoapServer::handle() (xmlGetIntSubset() != NULL) now actually sees the
DTD and rejects such requests, as on upstream.

Differences from upstream: 5.6 cleanup_xml_node() frees via a deferred
`del` pointer instead of an inline unlink/free, so the empty
XML_DTD_NODE branch is added before the non-element `del = trav` branch;
same effect. Test GHSA-4646-p932-gw34.phpt: array() instead of [], soap
checked in SKIPIF instead of --EXTENSIONS-- (needs php-cgi for --POST--).

Not compiled or tested yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/soap/php_xml.c                      |  3 +++
 ext/soap/tests/GHSA-4646-p932-gw34.phpt | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ext/soap/tests/GHSA-4646-p932-gw34.phpt

diff --git a/ext/soap/php_xml.c b/ext/soap/php_xml.c
index f3b49dfd..e8d78600 100644
--- a/ext/soap/php_xml.c
+++ b/ext/soap/php_xml.c
@@ -55,6 +55,9 @@ static void cleanup_xml_node(xmlNodePtr node)
 			if (is_blank(trav->content)) {
 				del = trav;
 			}
+		} else if (trav->type == XML_DTD_NODE) {
+			/* Attribute-value entity references can share content with the DTD.
+			 * Keep it alive until the document itself is freed. */
 		} else if ((trav->type != XML_ELEMENT_NODE) &&
 		           (trav->type != XML_CDATA_SECTION_NODE)) {
 			del = trav;
