From b7973ae89dddad4a77636fe8a6da8aa85e32948c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:54:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 (CVE-2026-129538): PATH_INFO
 underflow in CGI init_request_info()

Backport of php-src 1e109bfbd2 ("Fix GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564: PATH_INFO
underflow in CGI init_request_info()", PHP-8.2).

With cgi.fix_pathinfo=1, when the suffix stripped from SCRIPT_FILENAME
(or PATH_TRANSLATED) was longer than PATH_INFO, the re-derived
path_info pointed before the PATH_INFO value and was then read,
written (path_info[0] = 0) and copied from. Only rewrite PATH_INFO when
it is longer than the stripped suffix.

Differences from upstream: 5.6 uses int slen/pilen instead of size_t
(the comparison `pilen > slen` is between two non-negative ints); the
hunk is otherwise identical. php-cgi only - FPM gets the equivalent
CVE-2019-11043 check in a separate commit.
Test ghsa-5j3f-64r7-f564.phpt: proc_open() with a command string
(array form is 7.4+), isset() ternaries instead of `??`, no typed
params, Windows SystemRoot passthrough dropped.

Not compiled or tested yet.

