From 44ede02e1248474021862b80972e51622ac45787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:55:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #78599 (CVE-2019-11043): env_path_info underflow in
 FPM init_request_info()

Port of the FPM part of php-src ab061f95ca ("Fix bug #78599
(env_path_info underflow can lead to RCE) (CVE-2019-11043)"), released
in 7.1.33/7.2.24/7.3.11 after 5.6 went EOL, so 5.6.40 never got it.
Same root cause as GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 in php-cgi (previous commit).

With cgi.fix_pathinfo=1 (the default), a SCRIPT_FILENAME suffix longer
than PATH_INFO (e.g. nginx fastcgi_split_path_info with a %0a in the
URL, leaving PATH_INFO empty) made path_info point before the
PATH_INFO value; init_request_info() then wrote a NUL there
(path_info[0] = 0) - the known remote code execution in php-fpm.
Only rewrite PATH_INFO when it is longer than the stripped suffix.

The two lines are taken verbatim from 7.4.33 sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_main.c
(:1143-1144); the 5.6 code around them is the same (int slen/pilen,
apache_was_here branch untouched).
Test: upstream sapi/fpm/tests/bug78599-path-info-underflow.phpt
rewritten for the 5.6 FPM harness (include.inc/run_request instead of
FPM\Tester).

Not compiled or tested yet.

