From 28cbbbef1ad8fb3ac9126de794e039bbe0de344c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #81727 (CVE-2022-31629): cookie names mangled into
 __Host-/__Secure-

PHP turns "." and " " in variable names into "_", so a cookie named
"..Host-x" arrived as "__Host-x". A cookie set by a sibling subdomain or
over plain HTTP could then pose as a __Host-/__Secure- cookie, which
browsers only accept from the exact secure origin. Such names are now
discarded when the unmangled name did not have the prefix.

Backport of php-src 0611be4e82 (Derick Rethans), same change as Sury's 5.6
patch 0199. The NEWS hunk is left out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/standard/tests/bug81727.phpt | 15 +++++++++++++++
 main/php_variables.c             | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ext/standard/tests/bug81727.phpt

diff --git a/ext/standard/tests/bug81727.phpt b/ext/standard/tests/bug81727.phpt
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..71a9cb46
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ext/standard/tests/bug81727.phpt
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+--TEST--
+Bug #81727: $_COOKIE name starting with ..Host/..Secure should be discarded
+--COOKIE--
+..Host-test=ignore; __Host-test=correct; . Secure-test=ignore; . Elephpant=Awesome;
+--FILE--
+<?php
+var_dump($_COOKIE);
+?>
+--EXPECT--
+array(2) {
+  ["__Host-test"]=>
+  string(7) "correct"
+  ["__Elephpant"]=>
+  string(7) "Awesome"
+}
diff --git a/main/php_variables.c b/main/php_variables.c
index 35ef3578..1049c33e 100644
--- a/main/php_variables.c
+++ b/main/php_variables.c
@@ -106,6 +106,20 @@ PHPAPI void php_register_variable_ex(char *var_name, zval *val, zval *track_vars
 	}
 	var_len = p - var;
 
+	/* Discard variable if mangling made it start with __Host-, where pre-mangling it did not start with __Host- */
+	if (strncmp(var, "__Host-", sizeof("__Host-")-1) == 0 && strncmp(var_name, "__Host-", sizeof("__Host-")-1) != 0) {
+		zval_dtor(val);
+		free_alloca(var_orig, use_heap);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* Discard variable if mangling made it start with __Secure-, where pre-mangling it did not start with __Secure- */
+	if (strncmp(var, "__Secure-", sizeof("__Secure-")-1) == 0 && strncmp(var_name, "__Secure-", sizeof("__Secure-")-1) != 0) {
+		zval_dtor(val);
+		free_alloca(var_orig, use_heap);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (var_len==0) { /* empty variable name, or variable name with a space in it */
 		zval_dtor(val);
 		free_alloca(var_orig, use_heap);
From 8b5917c302c9db8b24fad5d7c3c3d60e042b37df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-wpj3-hf5j-x4v4 (CVE-2024-2756): __Host-/__Secure-
 cookie bypass

The CVE-2022-31629 fix rejected a variable whose name only started with
__Host- or __Secure- after name mangling, but it checked too early: later
mangling of array names (for example "[__Host-" inside brackets) could
still produce such a name. A cookie set by a sibling subdomain or over
plain HTTP could then pose as a __Host-/__Secure- cookie. The check now
runs right before the variable is added.

Backport of php-src 093c08af25 (Niels Dossche), same change as Sury's 5.6
patch 0218.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
