From 369ebd5ff65c5e8d842e4db12ffbe375aab26a88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bugs #78875 and #78876 (CVE-2019-11048): multipart
 lengths in signed ints

The multipart/form-data parser kept read lengths and the length of an
array variable name in signed ints. A very long file name or variable
name overflowed them, which made PHP try to allocate huge amounts of
memory and abort, leaving its temporary upload files behind. The lengths
are now unsigned.

Backport of the main/rfc1867.c part of php-src 1c9bd513ac and 3c8582ca4b
(Christoph M. Becker), same change as Sury's 5.6 patch 0146 ("Backports
from 7.2.31"). The NEWS hunk is left out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
