Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #79099 (CVE-2020-7059): strip_tags() reads before the
 buffer

php_strip_tags_ex() looked at the byte before the current one (*(p-1))
in several states without checking that there is one, so crafted input
made strip_tags() and fgetss() read one byte before the buffer. Each of these checks now tests p >= buf + 1 first.

Backport of php-src 0f79b1bf30 and 2dc170e25d (Stanislav Malyshev), same
change as Sury's 5.6 patches 0123 and 0127.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
