From d89a58c79e1f2b0ad849900af59d7f9521785ec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CVE-2026-9672: bundled libgd GIF LZW decoder works on
 stale table data

On a clear code the GIF reader's LZW decoder reset table[1][0] instead of
table[1][i], and it carried on after a corrupt code stream, so a crafted
GIF made it work on stale or uninitialised table data. The decoder state
is now zero-initialised, the table is reset correctly and a corrupt code
stream ends decoding. PHP built with the bundled libgd (as Gentoo's
ebuild builds it) reaches this through imagecreatefromgif().

Backport of php-src fcd691b377 (Ilija Tovilo; patch by Pierre Joye).
Sury has no 5.6 version of it; his 7.4 patch 0139 applies to this tree
unchanged (ext/gd/libgd/gd_gif_in.c is the same code here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
