From 7fe06711affa07b1eddd61d6792e141ef0e5e4cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mitigate GHSA-76gg-c692-v2mw (CVE-2023-3247): SoapClient HTTP
 Digest cnonce

The client nonce for HTTP Digest auth was the MD5 of one php_rand()
value, so it had only as many random bits as one call returns. It is now
built from four php_rand() values.

This is the minimal variant by Remi Collet (php-src 66e67c73b8), same
change as Sury's 5.6 patch 0210. The full upstream fix uses 16 bytes
from the CSPRNG (php_random_bytes), which only exists since PHP 7.0, so
on 5.6 the cnonce has more random bits but still does not come from a
cryptographic source. The NEWS hunk is left out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/soap/php_http.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/soap/php_http.c b/ext/soap/php_http.c
index 32460919..f3935cb1 100644
--- a/ext/soap/php_http.c
+++ b/ext/soap/php_http.c
@@ -639,10 +639,13 @@ try_again:
 					char          HA1[33], HA2[33], response[33], cnonce[33], nc[9];
 					PHP_MD5_CTX   md5ctx;
 					unsigned char hash[16];
+					int i;
 
