From 38ddf1a42c10827d53d0675526966705846500d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-453j-q27h-5p8x (CVE-2025-6491): SoapVar with a name
 over 2 GB

libxml2 before 2.13 leaves a node with a NULL name when xmlNodeSetName()
gets a name longer than 2 GB, and serialising the message then
dereferences it. The name is reset to a sentinel in that case. With
libxml2 2.13 and later the bug cannot happen; the change is harmless
there.

Backport of php-src 9cb3d8d200 (Ahmed Lekssays), with Sury's change of the
test for 5.6 (no return types); same change as Sury's 5.6 patch 0283 and
the soap_qname_crash.phpt parts of 0314 and 0317 (the test skips on
5.6: its strings cannot pass 2 GB, so it cannot build the input).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
