From 6e0a4f456145a6dd2d70d4dc0361f6133dcb8f19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-85c2-q967-79q5 (CVE-2026-6722): stale SOAP ref_map
 pointer with Apache Map

SOAP_GLOBAL(ref_map) stored decoded values for href lookups without
holding a reference. When decoding an Apache Map freed such a value, a
later lookup used the freed zval: a use-after-free reachable from a SOAP
message (SoapServer request or SoapClient response). The map now holds a
reference and releases it when it is reset.

Backport of php-src aee3b3ac9b (Ilija Tovilo), with Sury's 5.6 follow-up:
parse_packet_soap() copied the decoded result out of its zval and freed
that zval, which ref_map may still reference; it now copies the value
and drops its own reference instead. Same change as Sury's 5.6 patches
0292 and 0316, and the test part of 0370 (SKIPIF instead of
--EXTENSIONS--, which this version's run-tests does not know).
r3_groupE_list_006w.phpt now expects the repeated href node as a plain
object, not a PHP reference (ref_map holds its own reference; same
object either way), as in Sury's 0317.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/soap/php_encoding.c                       |  5 ++
 ext/soap/php_packet_soap.c                    |  6 +-
 ext/soap/tests/GHSA-85c2-q967-79q5.phpt       | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../Round3/GroupE/r3_groupE_list_006w.phpt    |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 ext/soap/tests/GHSA-85c2-q967-79q5.phpt

diff --git a/ext/soap/php_encoding.c b/ext/soap/php_encoding.c
index a5473dd5..d08dce69 100644
--- a/ext/soap/php_encoding.c
+++ b/ext/soap/php_encoding.c
@@ -383,6 +383,11 @@ static zend_bool soap_check_xml_ref(zval **data, xmlNodePtr node TSRMLS_DC)
 				return 1;
 			}
 		} else {
+			/* Hold a reference, the value may be released (e.g. a duplicate Apache Map key)
+			   while it is still reachable through href. Only decoding stores zvals in the
+			   map, encoding stores xmlNodePtr, so the destructor is set here. */
+			Z_ADDREF_PP(data);
+			SOAP_GLOBAL(ref_map)->pDestructor = ZVAL_PTR_DTOR;
 			zend_hash_index_update(SOAP_GLOBAL(ref_map), (ulong)node, (void**)data, sizeof(zval*), NULL);
 		}
 	}
diff --git a/ext/soap/php_packet_soap.c b/ext/soap/php_packet_soap.c
index 2bcb042c..42c91167 100644
--- a/ext/soap/php_packet_soap.c
+++ b/ext/soap/php_packet_soap.c
@@ -387,8 +387,10 @@ int parse_packet_soap(zval *this_ptr, char *buffer, int buffer_size, sdlFunction
 			tmp = *(zval**)tmp;
 			Z_ADDREF_P(tmp);
 			zval_dtor(return_value);
-			*return_value = *tmp;
-			FREE_ZVAL(tmp);
+			/* tmp may still be referenced from SOAP_GLOBAL(ref_map), so it must not be freed here */
+			ZVAL_COPY_VALUE(return_value, tmp);
+			zval_copy_ctor(return_value);
+			zval_ptr_dtor(&tmp);
 		}
 	}
 
