From f3c039b16ccd3d8c3cf648e3d007744a0dfe08cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-hmxp-6pc4-f3vv (CVE-2026-7262): NULL dereference on
 an Apache Map without value

The NULL check for a map item's value tested the wrong pointer, so a
crafted Apache Map in a SOAP message crashed the worker.

Backport of php-src 79551ab8b1 (Ilija Tovilo), same change as Sury's 5.6
patch 0253, and the test part of 0370 (SKIPIF instead of
--EXTENSIONS--).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
