From 6178945460d4a947aeed0654fca9ef58f2f6dfc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:21:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-c5f2-jwm7-mmq2 (CVE-2024-11234): CRLF injection via
 fulluri

With request_fulluri (always on through a proxy) the http wrapper put
the user's path into the request line as given, so CR/LF in it injected
headers or a second request towards the proxy. Such a path is now
refused ("HTTP wrapper full URI path does not allow CR or LF
characters"); the request_fulluri option is read before that check.

Backport of php-src 426a6d4539 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 5.6 patch 0234.
One context line differs: our GHSA-f6gg fix already compares the
scheme case-insensitively ("use_ssl = ... https").

