From 1004f9a54f2a743f5b8286915647ce6f5493ecb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:21:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix #79265: Host and other headers checked only at their
 first match

To decide whether the user already set Host, User-Agent, From,
Authorization, Content-Length or Content-Type, the http wrapper looked
only at the first occurrence of the name in the header bag. With
"X-Forwarded-Host: a" before "Host: b" the first match is inside the
other header, so PHP added its own Host and the request carried two.
Every occurrence is now checked, and a name counts only after a line
break, not after any space or tab.

Backport of php-src d0d60503b5 (Miguel Xavier Penha Neto) with its
follow-ups 3d9c02364d and 56cdbe63c2 (Nikita Popov), Sury's 5.6
patches 0274-0276. The GHSA-hgf5 fix below changes this same check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
