From 606f1f65bb55bbdcfff69268b4601ee90e448bce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:21:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: an http ServerClientTestCase.inc for the new http
 tests

The GHSA-hgf5 tests (and the GHSA-v8xr, -pcmh and -52jp tests below)
come from branches whose openssl ServerClientTestCase.inc supports
ephemeral ports (phpt_notify_server_start()). 5.6's does not, so this
adds the 7.4 helper as ext/standard/tests/http/ServerClientTestCase.inc,
without scalar and return type declarations, and the hgf5 tests include
it. 5.6 writes the request in several parts, so their server reads up
to the blank line instead of doing one fread(). Test change only.

Sury's 5.6 patches 0278-0280 and 0318.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
