From 210b6a808a9b0c81758ca29f68ea6ccac696a7e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:21:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g (CVE-2025-1217): http response header
 folding

The http wrapper treated a folded (continuation) response header line
as a new header, so a server could smuggle a Location or Content-Type
past the parser. Folded lines are now joined onto the header they
continue, as RFC 7230 describes. A header line that starts with a bare
CR, or a folded line before any header, fails the request.

Our own port: Sury has no 5.6 patch for it. It follows php-src
d20b4c97a9 (Jakub Zelenka) as in Sury's 7.2 patch 0176, in the 5.6
API. 5.6 still matched "Location: " and the other headers literally, so
the parser comes with the 7.x header matching (bug #47021): the name
up to the colon, optional whitespace, then the value, trailing
whitespace stripped; Transfer-Encoding chunked is recognised without
regard to case. follow_location keeps 5.6's integer conversion. The
header state is set up before the first "goto out", and a dechunk
filter is still freed when the request fails. The tests use the http
ServerClientTestCase.inc added above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
