From 1d0b583320e938881fbb7df3ff78ad0a3e8a38b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:21:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix out-of-bounds read on an empty Location header (GH-23467)

Since the GHSA-52jp change above an empty Location allocates one byte
and is followed, and the relative-redirect branch read location[1]
past it, so a server could make the client follow a redirect built
from heap garbage. The branch now uses the stored length and skips the
join for an empty Location. The follow-up GH-23521 keeps the old
handling of a one-character Location (resolved against the host root,
as before).

Our own port: Sury has no 5.6 patch for it. It follows php-src
547566f17a (Ilia Alshanetsky) and 64664758cd (Jordi Kroon) as in
Sury's 7.2 patches 0180 and 0181.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
